stream
BT
/F1 11 Tf
14 TL
56 760 Td
(Platform Runbook - Incident Response) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Severity Levels) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SEV1 - Complete outage or data loss. Page the on-call lead immediately.) Tj T*
(       Target acknowledgement: 5 minutes. Status page update: 15 minutes.) Tj T*
(SEV2 - Major degradation affecting many customers. Acknowledge in 15) Tj T*
(       minutes. Status page update within 30 minutes.) Tj T*
(SEV3 - Minor degradation or a single-customer issue. Handle during) Tj T*
(       business hours. No status page update required.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Escalation) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The primary on-call engineer owns the incident until it is resolved or) Tj T*
(formally handed over. If the primary does not acknowledge a SEV1 page) Tj T*
(within 10 minutes, PagerDuty automatically escalates to the secondary,) Tj T*
(and after a further 10 minutes to the engineering manager.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Rollback Procedure) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Deployments are rolled back with: orbctl release rollback --env prod) Tj T*
(--to-previous. A rollback takes about 4 minutes to propagate across all) Tj T*
(regions. Database migrations are NOT reversed by a rollback and must be) Tj T*
(reverted separately using the down migration.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Always post the rollback in #incidents before running it.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
